14:11.778 --> 14:14.179
Absolutely, but I need
to say something first.

14:14.181 --> 14:16.614
Things are going
to be different this time.

14:16.616 --> 14:18.917
I'm not going to make
the same mistakes I made before.

14:18.919 --> 14:20.552
And I'm going to start
by showing you

14:20.554 --> 14:23.388
how much I appreciate you
every single day.

14:23.390 --> 14:26.391
Oh, that's really sweet, but
we really should talk about...

14:26.393 --> 14:30.461
♪ Who we should invite
to the wedding! ♪

14:33.632 --> 14:35.867
Hey.
Hi.

14:35.869 --> 14:37.635
Guess what.
I'm taking your advice,

14:37.637 --> 14:40.839
and I'm surprising Brooke
with a romantic evening.

14:40.841 --> 14:43.675
Good. You know, I know
that's not easy for you.

14:43.677 --> 14:45.210
Your dad was the same way.

14:45.212 --> 14:48.880
His idea of romance
was a warm washcloth,

14:48.882 --> 14:52.283
cab fare
and a bottle of penicillin.

14:52.285 --> 14:56.654
Aw! So my dad wasn't just
a drunken, diseased man-whore.

14:56.656 --> 14:59.324
He was a gentleman.

14:59.326 --> 15:04.095
Charlie would be so happy
to see his little girl now.

15:04.097 --> 15:06.130
Of course,
he'd be even more happy

15:06.132 --> 15:08.566
to see the rack
on his little girl's girlfriend.

15:08.568 --> 15:10.268
Does she have nice boobs?

15:10.270 --> 15:13.137
I've never noticed.

15:13.139 --> 15:14.572
Hey.

15:14.574 --> 15:16.040
Oh, hey.

15:16.042 --> 15:18.643
How'd it go with Judith?
She take it okay?

15:18.645 --> 15:20.712
Uh, well, uh, you know,
she... uh, she...

15:20.714 --> 15:23.381
It was a... a little hard
for her to swallow.

15:23.383 --> 15:24.816
Um...

15:24.818 --> 15:27.151
Well, I'm just glad
you talked to her.

15:27.153 --> 15:28.786
Can I get my ring back?

15:28.788 --> 15:30.021
Uh, funny story.

15:30.023 --> 15:32.490
Um... she kind of kept it,

15:32.492 --> 15:34.325
and we're kind of
getting married.

15:35.728 --> 15:37.962
Alan, I thought
you were gonna talk to her.

15:37.964 --> 15:39.197
Uh, I did.

15:39.199 --> 15:41.466
Uh, we came to an...
oral agreement.

15:41.468 --> 15:43.835
Oh!

15:43.837 --> 15:44.969
Alan!

15:44.971 --> 15:46.137
It's my weakness.

15:46.139 --> 15:47.472
That and red velvet anything.

15:47.474 --> 15:48.673
Wait. Wait.

15:48.675 --> 15:50.275
This is the same woman

15:50.277 --> 15:52.343
that you said was so evil

15:52.345 --> 15:55.546
that her image didn't show up
in your wedding pictures.

15:55.548 --> 15:57.415
I only said that because,
at the time,

15:57.417 --> 15:59.817
I thought she was
the worst person I'd ever met,

15:59.819 --> 16:01.886
and she made my life
a living hell.

16:01.888 --> 16:03.087
But, you know, people change.

16:03.089 --> 16:04.756
It's gonna be great.

16:06.959 --> 16:11.029
So, Zippy's moving out,
and he's going to be miserable.

16:11.031 --> 16:12.997
So you &lt;i>have&lt;/i>
been listening.

16:12.999 --> 16:15.166
Oh.

16:16.001 --> 16:17.969
Oh, say,

16:17.971 --> 16:19.170
dinner was great, Judith.

16:19.172 --> 16:20.438
Thank you for inviting me over.

16:20.440 --> 16:22.473
Of course. You're
Alan's best friend.

16:22.475 --> 16:24.375
Actually, you're
Alan's &lt;i>only&lt;/i> friend.

16:24.377 --> 16:26.077
(laughter)

16:26.079 --> 16:27.545
It's funny 'cause it's true.

16:27.547 --> 16:29.213
(laughter)

16:29.215 --> 16:30.982
Oh, honey, uh, could you pass
the potatoes, please?

16:30.984 --> 16:33.918
Oh, I think you've already
had plenty, doughboy. Mm.

16:33.920 --> 16:35.586
(high-pitched):
Ah-ha.

16:35.588 --> 16:36.688
(laughs)

16:36.690 --> 16:38.923
Well, I have to say,

16:38.925 --> 16:42.160
I was shocked when Alan told me
you were getting married again.

16:42.162 --> 16:43.728
Oh, you were shocked?

16:43.730 --> 16:45.596
There was a time
when just the thought

16:45.598 --> 16:47.699
of being touched by his tiny,
clammy hands again

16:47.701 --> 16:49.767
made me throw up
in my mouth a little.

16:49.769 --> 16:50.969
(laughs)

16:50.971 --> 16:52.203
That's all ancient history.

16:52.205 --> 16:55.873
Yeah, if ancient history
was last Thursday.

16:55.875 --> 16:57.775
(Judith and Alan laugh)

16:57.777 --> 16:58.910
(both making kissing sound)

16:58.912 --> 17:01.346
Oh, isn't she great?

17:01.348 --> 17:02.880
No!

17:03.716 --> 17:04.849
She's treating you like crap.

17:04.851 --> 17:06.718
The only people
that get to do that

17:06.720 --> 17:08.686
are people
that do it out of love,

17:08.688 --> 17:10.688
like me and Berta and your mom.

17:10.690 --> 17:12.457
Okay, fine. Me and Berta.

17:13.092 --> 17:15.026
Okay. Me.

17:15.028 --> 17:16.260
It's harmless.

17:16.262 --> 17:17.895
It's just Judith being funny.

17:17.897 --> 17:21.299
Did... did you just twitch?

17:21.301 --> 17:24.802
No, I was just talking
about how funny Judith is.

17:24.804 --> 17:26.237
Okay, look me in the eye

17:26.239 --> 17:28.740
and tell me how much you love
Judith without twitching.

17:28.742 --> 17:30.942
Fine. I love Judith.

17:31.744 --> 17:33.578
There, I said it.

17:33.580 --> 17:34.979
Alan.

17:35.714 --> 17:37.615
You cannot marry this woman.

17:37.617 --> 17:38.950
You deserve better.

17:38.952 --> 17:40.952
I mean, not much better,
but better.

17:40.954 --> 17:42.053
You know who I deserve?

17:42.055 --> 17:43.921
I deserve Lyndsey,
but I can't have her.

17:43.923 --> 17:46.424
She's marrying somebody else,
so I'm taking what I can get.

17:46.426 --> 17:48.259
That's what I do.
I'm a love scavenger.

17:48.261 --> 17:51.429
You're also a house scavenger
and a money scavenger

17:51.431 --> 17:53.097
and an underwear scavenger.

17:53.099 --> 17:55.066
But that doesn't mean
you have to settle.

17:55.068 --> 17:56.667
Yes, it does.
I don't want to die alone.

17:56.669 --> 17:58.736
Maybe you don't realize it,
but there aren't a lot of people

17:58.738 --> 18:00.671
who want to spend the rest
of their lives with me.

18:00.673 --> 18:03.074
Oh, no, I realize it!

18:06.745 --> 18:08.913
Brooke, really, we can get
a hotel for the night.

18:08.915 --> 18:10.214
No, no, no, Dad.
It's fine.

18:10.216 --> 18:12.450
I'll sleep on the couch,
and you guys stay in my room.

18:13.585 --> 18:16.120
Surprise!

18:16.122 --> 18:18.222
Who's this?

18:18.224 --> 18:21.159
Uh, Mom, Dad,
this is, um...

18:21.161 --> 18:22.860
my girlfriend, Jenny.

18:22.862 --> 18:25.730
It's a pleasure to meet you!

18:25.732 --> 18:28.132
I like her.

18:31.703 --> 18:34.138
Oh, hey, I was thinking,
now that Jake's gone...

18:34.140 --> 18:37.141
Mm? - ...I can turn his room
into my man-cave. You know, a

18:37.143 --> 18:40.478
pinball machine, flat-screen
TV, potter's wheel.

18:40.480 --> 18:42.113
No, that's not going to happen.

18:42.115 --> 18:43.214
Oh, you have
plans for it?

18:43.216 --> 18:44.348
No, I'm just not

18:44.350 --> 18:46.050
letting you get
another potter's wheel.

18:47.719 --> 18:48.886
(laughs)

18:48.888 --> 18:50.288
Judith, I have to say,

18:50.290 --> 18:52.090
I cannot take my eyes off
of that ring.

18:52.092 --> 18:53.958
I know. When I first saw it,

18:53.960 --> 18:55.393
I thought it was as fake
as the orgasms

18:55.395 --> 18:56.761
I used to have
when we were married.

18:56.763 --> 18:57.929
(laughs)

18:57.931 --> 18:59.197
That's true.

18:59.199 --> 19:00.398
Very unsatisfactory lover.

19:00.400 --> 19:01.799
(Judith laughs)

19:01.801 --> 19:03.434
JUDITH:
But I mean,

19:03.436 --> 19:05.403
what woman could say no to this?

19:05.405 --> 19:06.838
I can think of one.

19:08.474 --> 19:09.974
Can you think of one, Alan?

19:11.510 --> 19:13.511
Uh, what's going on?

19:13.513 --> 19:14.912
Oh, nothing. I'm just glad

19:14.914 --> 19:17.115
that you were there
to pick up the pieces

19:17.117 --> 19:18.716
after Lyndsey turned down
Alan's proposal.

19:18.718 --> 19:21.119
What?! You proposed
to her before me?

19:21.121 --> 19:22.653
Uh, well, technically,
uh, what I...

19:22.655 --> 19:24.255
Oh, you didn't know?

19:25.858 --> 19:28.259
This is awkward.

19:28.261 --> 19:32.597
Open mouth, remove pie,
insert foot.

19:32.599 --> 19:34.565
So, I'm your second choice?!

19:34.567 --> 19:36.601
No, d-doesn't matter
who was second.

19:36.603 --> 19:39.237
Uh, y-you were the
first to say yes!

19:40.105 --> 19:41.572
I will be the first

19:41.574 --> 19:44.275
to say yes
to seconds of this pie.

19:44.277 --> 19:45.343
You are unbelievable!

19:45.345 --> 19:46.444
No, the important thing is

19:46.446 --> 19:47.845
that we found
each other again.

19:47.847 --> 19:49.413
And you're willing
to settle for me,

19:49.415 --> 19:51.115
and I'm willing
to settle for you.

19:51.117 --> 19:52.283
Settle for this.

19:52.285 --> 19:54.452
Oh! God!

19:57.456 --> 19:59.790
I'm a good friend.

19:59.792 --> 20:01.759
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

20:08.458 --> 20:10.058
Hey. How's it going?

20:10.426 --> 20:12.560
Good. Thanks again
for the potter's wheel.

20:13.062 --> 20:14.528
It's the least I could do.

20:14.530 --> 20:15.863
I cost you a wife.

20:15.865 --> 20:16.930
I'm just glad

20:16.932 --> 20:18.265
you, uh, came to your senses.

20:18.267 --> 20:19.500
Yeah, I was just scared.

20:19.502 --> 20:21.635
Didn't want to spend the rest
of my life alone.

20:21.637 --> 20:25.139
Hey, as long as I'm around,
you'll never be alone.

20:25.141 --> 20:26.840
Ah, thanks, buddy.

20:26.842 --> 20:27.908
Oh, shoot. Aah!

20:27.910 --> 20:30.144
Oh, here. Let me help
you out with that.

20:30.146 --> 20:32.312
Oh.

20:50.298 --> 20:53.433
(yells)

20:53.435 --> 20:56.737
Thank God, it was just a dream.

20:56.739 --> 20:59.339
Are you okay, baby?
Did you have a nightmare?

20:59.341 --> 21:01.508
(yells)

21:04.028 --> 21:07.264
(sighs)
I got to get him out of here.

21:07.266 --> 21:12.266
